  "scope": "Standard UART0-4, HP I2C0-1, SPI2 standard master, LEDC channels, ADC1, RMT channels and I2S master only; other SPI hosts, LP and high-speed modes not modeled. P4 datasheet lists a second ADC controller but its external channels are not identified in the GPIO summary, so ADC2 is not modeled. RMT channels are modeled as one GPIO per channel without TX/RX direction.\n\nDisplay/Camera peripherals: (1) camera0 = DVP 8-bit Camera interface routed through GPIOMatrix (same as ESP32-S3 LCD_CAM CAM DVP channel). (2) camera1 = MIPI CSI-2 2-lane receiver with dedicated differential pads: CLKP/CLKN + DATAP0/DATAN0 (lane 0 required for 1-lane mode), DATAP1/DATAN1 (lane 1 optional for 2-lane mode), refclk (output from P4, optional GPIO) and xclk/csi_enable/dvp_enable (optional GPIO-level control pads). MIPI pads are in VDD_MIPI_DPHY dedicated I/O domain, NOT routable through GPIOMatrix. (3) lcd0 = RGB LCD parallel interface (same as ESP32-S3 LCD_CAM, up to 24-bit d0-d23 + pclk/vsync/hsync/de), GPIOMatrix routed. (4) lcd1 = MIPI DSI 4-lane (clock lane + 4 data lanes), DPHY dedicated differential pads with dedicated I/O domain; lane 0 required for 1-lane mode, lanes 1/2/3 optional for wider busses; te (Tearing Effect) input and reset optional GPIO. ISP/H.264 and LP_CAM are not modeled here. twai0-twai2 model the three TWAI (CAN) controllers (TX/RX required, BUS-OFF/CLKOUT optional) routed through GPIOMatrix; an external transceiver is required. sdmmc1 models SDMMC host slot 1, which is GPIOMatrix-routed (any GPIO) with a 1-bit baseline clk/cmd/d0 and an optional 4-bit extension d1-d3; slot 0 is dedicated to UHS-I and is not GPIO-matrix routable, so it is not modeled.",
